  "regression": {
    "classification": "confirmed-valid-SDK-message-ingress-and-restart-regression",
    "trigger": "TDLib messageCustomServiceAction has content.text:string. Generic formattedText check added since baseline rejects it. Historical accept stores complete message and classifier handles content type as service with empty extracted text. New admission rejected before inbox insert; pending historical row was marked needs_review on restart.",
    "beforeEvidence": "Actual baseline accept/process functions, with imports rebound to current offline dependencies, accepted/routed13of13 representative shapes; current classifier routed12of13 and marked custom service action needs_review. Existing test extended with pre-upgrade persisted service row failed before fix: expected routed, got needs_review.",
    "fix": "Only permit string content.text when content._ is exactly messageCustomServiceAction; other text and caption checks unchanged. FilterMessage text union now includes string and consumer explicitly returns empty text for string. No service type added to MESSAGE_TYPES, no parser/trading/provider action enabled.",
    "afterEvidence": "Guard test proves both resumed and fresh service messages route again while malformed messageText string and photo caption string still reject; round-trip preserves full source payload. Baseline/current filter projections identical across100installed SDK MessageContent variants.",
    "limitations": "Restores durable admission/classification; does not assert Telegram permits forwarding every service type. No Telegram service/provider call performed. Existing downstream dispatch and rejection remains unchanged."
  },
  "producerAndMigrationTrace": [
    "forwarder.handleUpdate updateNewMessage -> routeIncomingMessage excludes outgoing and unauthorized source before accept; TDLib payload remains unprojected, JSON.stringify(message) stores full source object.",
    "acceptIncomingMessage still pins active workflow/parser resources before source inbox and incoming_work insertion inside database transaction; new guard executes before transaction. Historical pending rows created under same durable schema retain complete message_json.",
    "processIncomingWork reads pending rows and isolates parse/validation exceptions as needs_review; closeAlbum reads retained message_json for album members. Existing atomicity test verifies persisted text and album replay after process death and dedupe.",
    "db durable_ingress_pinned_workflow_ai_reservations migration explicitly puts legacy inbox rows without full provenance into needs_review and blocks legacy pending outbox replay; these null message_json rows are not admitted by automatic pending-row classification.",
    "forwarder legacy-media-buffer migration retains messages in separate media_group_buffer, not incoming_work.message_json; unrelated historical buffer replay provenance is not widened.",
    "Installed SDK uses media_album_id:string. Existing application media_group_id optional routing field and fixtures are retained unchanged; absence of media_group_id is accepted, media_album_id remains in persisted opaque payload. This review makes no new assertion about historical album field naming."
  ],
